\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces HA-Expert-Bench results (240 questions; means over graded items, with $n$ per cell as in Section~\ref {sec:experiments}). Bold marks the best score in each column. Three patterns organize the table: fine-tuning doubles the base model; retrieval on the \emph  {base} model outperforms the full training pipeline without it; and the combination underperforms retrieval alone on open and trap questions while posting the best quantitative score. On the 30 auto-graded items alone (no judge), the scores are 0.433 / 0.500 / 0.600 / 0.600, in the same cell order.}}{6}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main}{{3}{6}{HA-Expert-Bench results (240 questions; means over graded items, with $n$ per cell as in Section~\ref {sec:experiments}). Bold marks the best score in each column. Three patterns organize the table: fine-tuning doubles the base model; retrieval on the \emph {base} model outperforms the full training pipeline without it; and the combination underperforms retrieval alone on open and trap questions while posting the best quantitative score. On the 30 auto-graded items alone (no judge), the scores are 0.433 / 0.500 / 0.600 / 0.600, in the same cell order}{table.3}{}}
